          %h2#as_categories_with_one_object As categories with one object
          %p
            Just as the category of regular
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoids
            is equivalent to the category of locally small (i.e. Set-enriched) categories with one object, the category of monoids in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            (with the obvious morphisms) is equivalent to the category of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched categories
            with one object.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#preservation_by_lax_monoidal_functors Preservation by lax monoidal functors
          %p
            Monoid structure is preserved by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functors"} lax monoidal functors
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oplax+monoidal+functors"} oplax monoidal functors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal functor
            for more details.
          %h3#category_of_monoids Category of monoids
          %p
            For special properties of categories of monoids, see
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+monoids"} category of monoids
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
          #AssociativeAlgebras.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              A monoid in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+modules"} category of modules
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mi Mod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R Mod
              (over any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+ring"} ground ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              and equipped with the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+modules"} tensor product of modules
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+unital+algebra"} associative unital algebra
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
          #Rings.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              As the special case of Exp.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AssociativeAlgebras"}
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = \mathbb{Z}
              the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            %p
              A monoid object in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
              with the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+abelian+groups"} tensor product of abelian groups
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              As the special case of Exp.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AssociativeAlgebras"}
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo =
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = k
              a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %p
              A monoid object in the category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
              (over any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+vector+spaces"} tensor product of vector spaces
              is an
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+unital+algebra"} associative unital algebra
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %ul
            %li
              A monoid object in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              (with cartesian product as the tensor product) is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+monoid"} topological monoid
            %li
              A monoid object in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28Top%29"} Ho(Top)
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-monoid"} H-monoid
            %li
              A monoid object in the category of monoids (with cartesian product as the tensor product) is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid"} commutative monoid
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eckmann-Hilton+argument"} Eckmann-Hilton argument
            %li
              A monoid object in the category of complete join-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semilattice"}> semilattice
              s (with its tensor product that represents maps preserving joins in each variable separately) is a unital
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantale"} quantale
            %li
              The category of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+set"} pointed set
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absorption+monoid"} absorption monoid
            %li
              Given any monoidal category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}
              is called a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonoid"} comonoid
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              In a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocartesian+monoidal+category"} cocartesian monoidal category
            %li
              For any category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
              category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^C
              has a monoidal structure induced by composition of endofunctors, and a monoid object in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^C
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            These are examples of monoids internal to monoidal categories. More generally, given any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            and a chosen object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-category"} hom-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(a,a)
            has the structure of a monoidal category. So, the concept of monoid makes sense in any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %strong
              monoid in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            to be a monoid in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(a,a)
            for some object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            is the same as monad on a category.
          %p
            A monoid in a bicategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            may also be described as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
            of a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            with a single object.
